    "share_count_basis": "Units in issue at 30 Jun 2026: 2,446,173,860 (1H2026 results, EPU/DPU table). Held flat: management fees paid in units are charged in the AFFO stream instead; no buybacks; acquisitions are assumed equity/debt-funded at no accretion, so per-unit growth is organic only.",
    "owner_affo_build": "TTM Distributable Income (FY2025 268.051 - 1H2025 127.128 + 1H2026 150.668 = 291.6m) less Capex Reserves retained (2H2025 ~12.8m [DI 140.9 - 5.248c x ~2,441m units]; 1H2026 10.9m [DI 150.668 - distribution 139.775]) = 23.7m, less management fees paid in units 14.2m = 253.7m (10.37c/unit). 1H2026 annualised on the same basis = 261.8m (10.70c/unit), which is what year 1 (3.5% growth) lands on.",
    "historical_debt_memo": "Not deducted (AFFO is post-interest): borrowings 2,292.4m and cash 244.1m at 30 Jun 2026; aggregate leverage 34.0%; 71.2% of loans hedged; ICR 6.9x (5.1x on +100bp).",
    "wacc_rationale": "Cost of equity, SGD-based: 10y SGS ~2.2%, ERP 5.5%, beta ~0.95 for an externally managed, 34%-geared S-REIT with 43.5% single-tenant concentration = ~7.4%, rounded to 7.5% base; bull 7.0% (re-rating toward data-centre REIT peers), bear 8.5% (rate shock / tenant-concentration premium). No WACC: the flow is post-interest so it is capitalised at the cost of equity with net debt held at zero.",
    "lease_treatment": "Land-lease rents for Singapore leasehold sites are inside property expenses and hence inside DI. Lease-extension premiums (e.g. the $350m paid Dec-2025 for KDC SGP 7/8 tenure) are lumpy capital outlays not in DI; they are the reason terminal growth is held at or below inflation (finite tenure decays the perpetuity).",
    "nci_treatment": "Distributable Income is stated net of non-controlling interests (attributable to Unitholders), so no NCI deduction.",
    "notes": "MODEL: REIT AFFO capitalisation at cost of equity via the component engine. Routed by .claude/skills/dcf-methods/SKILL.md (REIT / property trust row): Keppel DC REIT is an externally managed S-REIT carrying data centres at IAS 40 fair value, so reported net income is dominated by revaluation gains (FY2025 NI 427.8m vs DI 268.1m) and owner-FCF/EBITDA/net debt do not mean what an operating-company DCF assumes. The stream is owner AFFO = Distributable Income - Capex Reserves - management fees paid in units, already after interest, tax and NCI. Engine mapping: base_revenue = owner AFFO, EBITDA margin 100%, SBC/D&A/capex/tax/WC all zero, discount rate = cost of equity, net debt = 0 (never subtract debt from a post-interest flow). No prior ticker memory entry; first valuation. Cross-check: NAV/unit 1.73 at 30 Jun 2026, so price is ~1.23x P/NAV; the 1H2026 annualised DPU (11.43c) gives a 5.4% yield at the current price.",
